cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TORX — a legacy LD_PRELOAD Tor shim, kept as a control group"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Anirudh
    email: 179838340+Anirudh958@users.noreply.github.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Anirudh958/Torx.git
abstract: >-
  Research artifact arguing that LD_PRELOAD is the wrong primitive for
  routing a process through Tor: a measured leak taxonomy (dns, udp,
  ipv6, tcp, udp-correctness), a committed evidence harness
  (tests/leak/results.jsonl, schema 2), and mapped detection rules for
  the residual leaks. The shim itself is legacy and intentionally
  unpatched; the netns/cgroup/nftables architecture it motivates is
  documented in THREAT_MODEL.md.
keywords:
  - tor
  - ld-preload
  - anonymity
  - network-namespace
  - leak-taxonomy
  - detection-engineering
